WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:06.080
Since debuting in 2017, Riverdale has pushed
the boundaries of network television by placing

00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:11.060
the familiar and formerly innocuous characters
of Archie Comics into increasingly outlandish

00:00:11.060 --> 00:00:11.940
plots.

00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:15.940
Season 4 is set to premiere in the fall of
2019, and we've got everything you need to

00:00:15.940 --> 00:00:16.940
know.

00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:23.000
The first season of Riverdale hit the CW as
a midseason addition in January 2017.

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:28.720
That first short set of 13 episodes proved
so popular that the CW brought the show back

00:00:28.730 --> 00:00:33.370
as quickly as possible, promoting it to a
fall debut for season number two with a full

00:00:33.370 --> 00:00:35.200
order of 22 episodes.

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:39.920
Beginning with season two and into season
three, Riverdale led off the CW's Wednesday

00:00:39.920 --> 00:00:42.360
night programming, airing at 8 p.m.

00:00:42.360 --> 00:00:46.940
That's not broken, so the network isn't going
to fix it: Riverdale will continue on its

00:00:46.940 --> 00:00:50.160
fourth season with that same Wednesdays at
8:00 time slot.

00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:56.100
On June 17, 2019, the official Riverdale Instagram
page gave fans the exact date when the show

00:00:56.100 --> 00:00:57.880
would return: October 9th.

00:00:57.880 --> 00:01:02.820
It will serve as the lead in to a similar
"old concept, new approach" mystery show:

00:01:02.820 --> 00:01:03.920
Nancy Drew.

00:01:04.220 --> 00:01:10.020
On March 4th, 2019, Riverdale cast member
Luke Perry died suddenly at the age of 52,

00:01:10.020 --> 00:01:11.560
shortly after suffering a stroke.

00:01:11.560 --> 00:01:16.100
The first episode to air after the passing
of the actor, who played Archie's sweet father

00:01:16.100 --> 00:01:23.380
Fred Andrews, came with a title card reading,
"In Memoriam: Luke Perry, 1966–2019."

00:01:23.380 --> 00:01:28.120
The final installment to feature Perry as
Andrews debuted in late April, with the actor's

00:01:28.120 --> 00:01:33.440
final scene being a one-on-one with Archie,
offering his boy words of guidance and encouragement.

00:01:33.440 --> 00:01:38.460
Riverdale writers didn't explicitly deal with
the fate of Fred in season three, but will

00:01:38.460 --> 00:01:39.440
in season four.

00:01:39.440 --> 00:01:46.060
On June 19th, 2019, showrunner Roberto Aguirre-Sacasa
tweeted out the title page of the script for

00:01:46.060 --> 00:01:50.890
the first episode of season four, and it's
titled "Chapter Fifty-Eight: In Memoriam."

00:01:50.890 --> 00:01:55.790
"Probably the most important episode of Riverdale
we'll do this year, if not ever.

00:01:55.790 --> 00:01:57.810
A tribute to our fallen friend.

00:01:57.810 --> 00:02:00.700
Thankful for this opportunity to honor Luke
&amp; Fred."

00:02:00.700 --> 00:02:04.480
This heavily implies that the Fred Andrews
character will be laid to rest.

00:02:04.480 --> 00:02:10.039
At San Diego Comic-Con 2019, Aguirre-Sacasa
announced that the episode would feature a

00:02:10.039 --> 00:02:14.800
special guest star: Shannen Doherty, Perry's
iconic screen partner from their "Dylan and

00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:17.060
Brenda" days on Beverly Hills, 90210.

00:02:17.320 --> 00:02:22.500
Apart from the tragic loss of Luke Perry as
Fred Andrews, the main cast of Riverdale will

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:23.940
all be back for season four.

00:02:23.940 --> 00:02:29.020
The series will also welcome some high-profile
guest stars, both familiar and brand-new.

00:02:29.020 --> 00:02:33.810
Archie's parents are divorced, and his mother
lived far away, so Molly Ringwald only appeared

00:02:33.810 --> 00:02:35.700
occasionally as Mary Andrews.

00:02:35.700 --> 00:02:39.380
With the loss of Perry, Ringwald will likely
up her involvement.

00:02:39.380 --> 00:02:43.040
Aguirre-Sacasa told TV Line in May of 2019,

00:02:43.040 --> 00:02:46.800
"We've talked about Molly having a bigger
presence next year to help her son."

00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:51.900
Chad Michael Murray will also return as Edgar
Evernever, the creepy yet charming leader

00:02:51.900 --> 00:02:56.880
of the Farm, the bizarre, organ-harvesting
cult that tore Betty's family apart.

00:02:56.880 --> 00:03:02.300
And on that subject, Wyatt Nash is set for
a recurring arc as Charles Smith, an FBI agent

00:03:02.300 --> 00:03:04.780
who also happens to be Betty's long-lost brother.

00:03:04.780 --> 00:03:10.240
At Riverdale High, teen TV veteran Kerr Smith
will play tough new school principal Mr. Honey.

00:03:10.240 --> 00:03:15.620
Sam Witwer, best known for his roles as Mr.
Hyde on Once Upon a Time and Agent Liberty

00:03:15.620 --> 00:03:19.990
on Supergirl, will join the show as a troubled
writing teacher who becomes a mentor figure

00:03:19.990 --> 00:03:24.020
for Jughead when the crown-wearing kid ships
off to a fancy prep school.

00:03:24.160 --> 00:03:29.100
The fourth season of Riverdale will also mark
its characters' fourth year at Riverdale High.

00:03:29.100 --> 00:03:33.340
Senior year is an important time for so many
teenagers, and it will be for Archie and the

00:03:33.340 --> 00:03:34.340
gang, too.

00:03:34.520 --> 00:03:38.980
It figures so large in their lives that regular,
normal high school stuff will take prominence

00:03:38.980 --> 00:03:41.320
in the action of Riverdale's upcoming episodes.

00:03:41.320 --> 00:03:45.360
Camila Mendes, who plays Veronica, told Entertainment
Weekly at Comic-Con,

00:03:45.370 --> 00:03:50.230
"Season four is definitely senior year, high
school-focused, more about relationships and

00:03:50.230 --> 00:03:51.230
those dynamics."

00:03:51.230 --> 00:03:56.250
Meanwhile, Jughead's time away from Riverdale
could prove problematic for his relationship

00:03:56.250 --> 00:04:00.260
with Betty, according to actor Cole Sprouse,
who told Entertainment Tonight,

00:04:00.260 --> 00:04:02.920
"[Jughead's] only back in Riverdale on the
weekends.

00:04:02.920 --> 00:04:07.720
I think that is going to inevitably put stress
on the relationship between Betty and Jughead.

00:04:07.720 --> 00:04:09.420
I think it might be a little bit tense.

00:04:09.420 --> 00:04:13.760
They might fall, turn away from each other,
only to come back together way stronger."

00:04:13.760 --> 00:04:19.109
But will teen drama supplant pitch-black plots
like the Black Hood's killing spree, or Archie's

00:04:19.109 --> 00:04:21.800
involvement in a deadly underground boxing
ring?

00:04:24.960 --> 00:04:25.860
"You're doin' great, Arch."

00:04:25.960 --> 00:04:27.320
"How many of these guys am I fighting?!"

00:04:27.700 --> 00:04:28.580
Not quite.

00:04:28.580 --> 00:04:33.040
Mendes added that Riverdale will certainly
explore "the mystery of what we saw at the

00:04:33.050 --> 00:04:38.099
end of season three": a bleak flash-forward
depicting a blood-soaked Archie, Betty, and

00:04:38.099 --> 00:04:39.099
Veronica.

00:04:39.099 --> 00:04:43.990
Lili Reinhart, who plays Betty, also promises
that early in Season 4, the show will introduce

00:04:43.990 --> 00:04:45.320
another major mystery.

00:04:45.620 --> 00:04:49.280
Riverdale can't always be about mystery-solving
teens in grave danger.

00:04:49.280 --> 00:04:53.580
Every so often, the series breaks the tension
with a fun high-concept episode.

00:04:53.580 --> 00:04:59.320
A 2018 installment flashed back to Riverdale
High twenty-something years ago, centering

00:04:59.330 --> 00:05:03.680
on the antics of the present-day adults of
Riverdale when they were teens, and portrayed

00:05:03.680 --> 00:05:05.840
by the show's young cast members.

00:05:05.840 --> 00:05:10.900
A few months later, a meta, self-referential
episode found Riverdale High's drama club

00:05:10.900 --> 00:05:14.820
staging a musical production of the high school
cult classic Heathers.

00:05:15.160 --> 00:05:21.020
"Now how in God's name is a play about teen
violence and suicide a good idea in Riverdale?"

00:05:21.280 --> 00:05:26.520
Riverdale Season 4 will offer at least one
such novelty installment: the fourth episode

00:05:26.530 --> 00:05:32.289
of the season, airing on October 30th, marks
the show's first ever Halloween-themed chapter.

00:05:32.289 --> 00:05:35.809
Aguirre-Sacasa mentioned it during the show's
Comic-Con panel, saying,

00:05:35.809 --> 00:05:40.889
"We've got a really fun, spooky episode for
everyone...I know what Archie's gonna be dressed

00:05:40.889 --> 00:05:44.720
as, and we're trying to get clearance on some
DC comic book characters."

00:05:44.720 --> 00:05:49.779
Considering that Riverdale shares a network
with DC's "Arrowverse" shows, we may be in

00:05:49.780 --> 00:05:52.800
for some tongue-in-cheek superhero-related
Halloween fun.

